   - **Vapor Pressure at 20°C:** 12.8 kPa (128 mmHg) (Relatively high)
   - **OSHA PEM:** 200 ppm
   - **Explanation:**  Methane has a relatively high vapor pressure, meaning it evaporates easily at room temperature. This high volatility contributes to its relatively low PEM.  
