The area of each paving stone is:
\[ 2.5 \times w = 2.5w \]
The total area of 165 paving sides is:
\[ 165 \times 2.5w = 412.5w \]
Since the total area of the paving sides equals the area of the courtyard:
\[ 412.5w = 825 \]
\[ w = \frac{825}{412.5} = 2 \]
The width of each paving stone is 2 meters.

