(ii)  
\[
\tau = \frac{m c_p}{h A} = \frac{1.2 \times 385}{56.8 \times 0.075} = 10.4 \text{ s}
\]  
\[
T(t) = T_\infty + (T_0 - T_\infty) e^{-t/\tau} = 20 + (345 - 20) e^{-5 \times 60 / 10.4} = 20 + 325 e^{-288.46} = 20 + 0 = 20^\circ \text{C}
\]  
The temperature after 5 minutes is approximately 20°C.  
(ii) Time to reach 50°C:  
\[
50 = 20 + (345 - 20) e^{-t/\tau} \implies 30 = 325 e^{-t/\tau} \implies e^{-t/\tau} = \frac{30}{325} = 0.0923
\]  
\[
\frac{t}{\tau} = \ln(0.0923) = -2.31 \implies t = 2.31 \times 10.4 = 24 \text{ s}
\]  
The time required to reach 50°C is approximately 24 seconds.  
(iii) Time constant:  
The time constant is \(\tau = 10.4\) s, as calculated above.  
(iv) Convective heat transfer coefficient for lumped parameter:  
The Biot number must be less than 0.1 for the lumped parameter model to be valid.  
\[
Bi = \frac{h L_c}{k} = \frac{h L_c}{k} < 0.1
\]  
For a sphere, \(L_c = R\). For a rectangular part, \(L_c\) is the characteristic length.  
